# What in this project was taken from somewhere else rather than written here, one path per
# line with the reason after a `#`. `toolkit/source_hygiene.py` and `toolkit/copied_strings.py`
# read this and say what they skipped, so a scan over "every source file" is not a hundred
# findings about somebody else's minified bundle.

src/main/resources/gui  # the three HTML shells the original's own web framework serves, byte for byte: RENDERING.md R3 says the interface a source has is the one a port ships
src/main/resources/openapi  # the two OpenAPI documents, which are the descriptions the screens above draw and were captured from the running original
src/main/resources/engine/healthcheck/opal.rego  # OPAL's own health-check rego template, reproduced exactly because the transaction log it renders is read by rules a deployment already has
